{%- comment -%}
  Muretto, introduced once at the foot of the page.

  The "Get started" tabs for Le Mans Ultimate and the Assetto Corsa games link
  down here, so this section is the only place the relay is explained and the only
  place its download link lives.

  TODO: the download URL is not final. Replace muretto_download_url below when it
  is; nothing else on the page points at the installer.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign muretto_download_url = '#' -%}
<section class="product-muretto" id="muretto">
  <h2 class="product-section-title">Muretto</h2>
  <div class="product-muretto-body">
    <p>
      Muretto is a small Windows tray app that runs on the PC
      alongside your sim titles, reads their telemetry and carries it to Guido over your home network.
    </p>
    <p>
      It runs in the tray with no window, starts itself when you log on, and automatically streams telemetry from
      any active session. No setup needed, no messing with your sim, no asking for admin rights.
      It's built with minimal footprint, to make sure it doesn't interfere with your sim's performance.
    </p>
    <p>
      It's a necessary Guido companion for Le Mans Ultimate, Assetto Corsa and Assetto Corsa Competizione. Gran
      Turismo 7 talks to Guido directly instead, and does not need it.
    </p>
    <div class="product-muretto-download">
      {%- comment -%}
        The platform rides inside the button rather than on a line beside it, so
        the label says what you get and where it runs in one read.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <a class="ds-btn ds-btn--primary" href="{{ muretto_download_url }}">
        {% svg 'icons/windows.svg' %} Download Muretto
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
